<http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "http://rdfweb.org/mailman/listinfo/rdfweb-dev",
                                                                                "http://www.w3.org/RDF/Interest/";
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/coverage> "world";
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Dan Brickley",
                                                                            "Libby Miller";
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> """\"An agent (e.g. person, group, software or physical artifact).\"  NOTE: We adopted this concept partially from the FOAF ontology. However, in our ontology the agent concept does not comprise the subclasses software and physical artifact. We decided to introduce this main concept in order to make the range of e.g. the attribute authors of a publication more general."""@en;
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml";
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/publisher> "Dan Brickley",
                                                                              "Libby Miller";
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Agent"@en;
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/type> "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class";
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                                  rdfs:comment """\"An agent (e.g. person, group, software or physical artifact).\"  NOTE: We adopted this concept partially from the FOAF ontology. However, in our ontology the agent concept does not comprise the subclasses software and physical artifact. We decided to introduce this main concept in order to make the range of e.g. the attribute authors of a publication more general.""";
                                  rdfs:label "Agent"@en.
<http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Document> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "http://www.w3.org/RDF/Interest/",
                                                                                   "http://rdfweb.org/mailman/listinfo/rdfweb-dev";
                                     <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/coverage> "world";
                                     <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Dan Brickley",
                                                                               "Libby Miller";
                                     <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> """Similar to the Agent concept, we have again decided to include a concept from the popular FOAF ontology. The FOAF Vocabulary Specification currently defines Document in a very loose way: \"The <link>foaf:Document</link> class represents those things which are, broadly conceived, 'documents'. ... We do not (currently) distinguish between physical and electronic documents, or between copies of a work and the abstraction those copies embody.\"
The intended use of this concept within the SWPortal ontology is to subsume everything that contains some sort of information and has been produced by some <link>foaf:Agent</link> An instance of Document can either refer to an electronic or physical thing, as long as it is adressable by means of a URI. Examples are a book written, or a picture taken by a person, but also a log file generated by a machine."""@en;
                                     <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml";
                                     <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/publisher> "Libby Miller",
                                                                                 "Dan Brickley";
                                     <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Document"@en;
                                     <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/type> "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class";
                                     a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                                     rdfs:comment """Similar to the Agent concept, we have again decided to include a concept from the popular FOAF ontology. The FOAF Vocabulary Specification currently defines Document in a very loose way: \"The <link>foaf:Document</link> class represents those things which are, broadly conceived, 'documents'. ... We do not (currently) distinguish between physical and electronic documents, or between copies of a work and the abstraction those copies embody.\"
The intended use of this concept within the SWPortal ontology is to subsume everything that contains some sort of information and has been produced by some <link>foaf:Agent</link> An instance of Document can either refer to an electronic or physical thing, as long as it is adressable by means of a URI. Examples are a book written, or a picture taken by a person, but also a log file generated by a machine.""";
                                     rdfs:label "Document"@en;
                                     rdfs:subClassOf swpo:Publication.
<http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Group> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "http://rdfweb.org/mailman/listinfo/rdfweb-dev",
                                                                                "http://www.w3.org/RDF/Interest/";
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/coverage> "world";
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Libby Miller",
                                                                            "Dan Brickley";
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> """\"A class of Agents. The foaf:Group classs represents a collection of individual agents (and may itself play the role of a <link>foaf:Agent</link>, i.e. something that can perform actions).\""""@en;
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml";
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/publisher> "Libby Miller",
                                                                              "Dan Brickley";
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Group"@en;
                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/type> "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class";
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                                  rdfs:comment """\"A class of Agents. The foaf:Group classs represents a collection of individual agents (and may itself play the role of a <link>foaf:Agent</link>, i.e. something that can perform actions).\"""";
                                  rdfs:label "Group"@en;
                                  rdfs:subClassOf <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent>.
<http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Organization> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "http://www.w3.org/RDF/Interest/",
                                                                                       "http://rdfweb.org/mailman/listinfo/rdfweb-dev";
                                         <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/coverage> "world";
                                         <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Dan Brickley",
                                                                                   "Libby Miller";
                                         <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> """\"The foaf:Organization class represents a kind of foaf:Agent corresponding to social institutions such as companies, societies, etc.\" As we consider an organization to be a group as well, we introduced a subclass <link>Organization</link> as a subclass of both <link>foaf:Organization</link> and <link>foaf:Group</link>. We added <link>foaf:Organization</link> to facilitate FOAF based agents to query our ontology."""@en;
                                         <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml";
                                         <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/publisher> "Dan Brickley",
                                                                                     "Libby Miller";
                                         <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> ""@en;
                                         <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/type> "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class";
                                         a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                                         rdfs:comment """\"The foaf:Organization class represents a kind of foaf:Agent corresponding to social institutions such as companies, societies, etc.\" As we consider an organization to be a group as well, we introduced a subclass <link>Organization</link> as a subclass of both <link>foaf:Organization</link> and <link>foaf:Group</link>. We added <link>foaf:Organization</link> to facilitate FOAF based agents to query our ontology.""";
                                         rdfs:label ""@en;
                                         rdfs:subClassOf <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent>.
<http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Person> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "http://rdfweb.org/mailman/listinfo/rdfweb-dev",
                                                                                 "http://www.w3.org/RDF/Interest/";
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/coverage> "world";
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Dan Brickley",
                                                                             "Libby Miller";
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> """\"A person. The foaf:Person class represents people. Something is a foaf:Person if it is a person. We don't nitpick about whether they're alive, dead, real or imaginary.\""""@en;
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml";
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/publisher> "Libby Miller",
                                                                               "Dan Brickley";
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Person"@en;
                                   <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/type> "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class";
                                   a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                                   rdfs:comment """\"A person. The foaf:Person class represents people. Something is a foaf:Person if it is a person. We don't nitpick about whether they're alive, dead, real or imaginary.\"""";
                                   rdfs:label "Person"@en;
                                   rdfs:subClassOf <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent>.
<http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Project> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "http://www.w3.org/RDF/Interest/",
                                                                                  "http://rdfweb.org/mailman/listinfo/rdfweb-dev";
                                    <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/coverage> "world";
                                    <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Dan Brickley",
                                                                              "Libby Miller";
                                    <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> """\"A project (a collective endeavour of some kind).\" Within the context of the SWPortal Ontology we specify <link>foaf:Project</link> as such: A project is an endeavour of a group which has a specific aim. As a project can also be individualized and can publish documents and the like, we model it as a subclass of foaf:Agent. It has members and inherits all properties of <link>foaf:Agent</link> and <link>foaf:Group</link>. Also, projects are usually funded."""@en;
                                    <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml";
                                    <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/publisher> "Libby Miller",
                                                                                "Dan Brickley";
                                    <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Project"@en;
                                    <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/type> "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class";
                                    a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
                                    rdfs:comment """\"A project (a collective endeavour of some kind).\" Within the context of the SWPortal Ontology we specify <link>foaf:Project</link> as such: A project is an endeavour of a group which has a specific aim. As a project can also be individualized and can publish documents and the like, we model it as a subclass of foaf:Agent. It has members and inherits all properties of <link>foaf:Agent</link> and <link>foaf:Group</link>. Also, projects are usually funded.""";
                                    rdfs:label "Project"@en;
                                    rdfs:subClassOf swpo:TemporaryGroup.
<http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/currentProject> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "http://rdfweb.org/mailman/listinfo/rdfweb-dev",
                                                                                         "http://www.w3.org/RDF/Interest/";
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/coverage> "world";
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator> "Dan Brickley",
                                                                                     "Libby Miller";
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description> """\"A current project this person works on.\" NOTE: FOAF defines the range as <link>foaf:Person</link> - we decided to change this to the more general <link>foaf:Agent</link>, since other types of Agents (e.g. a company) can also have projects.
We have also defined an inverse for this property (see <link>drivenBy</link>)."""@en;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/format> "application/rdf+xml";
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/publisher> "Libby Miller",
                                                                                       "Dan Brickley";
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Current Project"@en;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/type> "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty";
                                           a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>;
                                           rdfs:comment """\"A current project this person works on.\" NOTE: FOAF defines the range as <link>foaf:Person</link> - we decided to change this to the more general <link>foaf:Agent</link>, since other types of Agents (e.g. a company) can also have projects.
We have also defined an inverse for this property (see <link>drivenBy</link>).""";
                                           rdfs:domain <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent>;
                                           rdfs:label "Current Project"@en;
                                           rdfs:range <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Project>;
                                           <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> swpo:drivenBy.
<http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/firstName> <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "http://www.w3.org/RDF/Interest/",
